## PR Title
Set up basic execution environment for running on DE1-SoC

## PR Description
Addresses issues #103 and #104 by establishing two separate execution environments for the project: one for simulation (used by testbenches and RISCOF) and one for the DE1-SoC FPGA deployment target. The core architectural change is extracting the memory (MA) out of the processor core, treating it as a peripheral rather than an internal component. The PR also lays down a basic memory map for the DE1-SoC platform with LEDR MMIO, demonstrating buildable and loadable code as a proof-of-concept. Memory currently infers as general logic; future work targets on-chip SRAM. Pending follow-ups: documentation for building/running on DE1-SoC and overall README/repository organization.

